{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfP3sYxC8PfGt613q7WSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 31 answers are computed and written to `/app/answers.json`. The three plan targets came out exactly equal to the widths my model produces for the minimal sets, which confirms the model matches the intended one.\n\n**What the archive says**\n\n- Every launched run is in one of five states: kept in `eval_results.csv`, screened out by the quality floor, lost with the w01 shard file, dropped by the w03/w07 sink outage, or dropped by the w09 late-campaign outage. Shard values from `recovered/` pin some of the outage and screened runs.\n- The recovery log covers only two states. Every shard-lost run came back as an exact value, and every screened run came back as a range whose width follows the suite: 0.04 for arc_lite, 0.02 for gsm_plus, 0.025 for code_ms. Neither sink-outage state appears, so a request on those runs guarantees nothing.\n- The daily digest is the key coupling. On the late campaign days it pins the sums so tightly that recovering the screened code_ms runs that finished those days is the only way to narrow the c4 and c5 means, even though those runs are in neither configuration.\n\n**Method**\n\nGuaranteed width for a contrast equals the maximum of the contrast difference between two consistent assignments, subject to each recovered screened run differing by at most its bucket width and each recovered shard-lost run being equal. That is a linear program per day, which I solved exactly in rational arithmetic and verified stays on the 0.0001 grid.\n\n**Results in brief**\n\n- Contrasts: k01 [-0.023209, 0.052085], k02 [-0.061141, 0.187956], k03 [-0.000775, 0.027796].\n- Recovery residuals: 0 for the shard-lost run, 0.025 for the three screened code_ms runs, and the full box width (0.75 or 1.0) for the outage runs.\n- Values: only v02 and v03 (shard-lost runs in the c0 dense greedy arm) are worth taking.\n- Plans: p01 needs 2 runs (r02612, r02613), p02 needs 1 (r02608), p03 needs 1 (r02612)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4472,"cache_read_input_tokens":67301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4472,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45429815-27c9-4e03-8f5e-cabcfdc01484","uuid":"da136098-bf01-49ac-a522-53f85a927030","timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:26:32.863Z"}
